Usage: agent-relay [options] [command]

Agent-to-agent messaging

Options:
  -V, --version        Output the version number
  -h, --help           display help for command

Commands:
  node                 Run and manage this machine's relay node
  version              Show version information
  update [options]     Check for updates and install if available
  uninstall [options]  Remove agent-relay data, configuration, and global
                       binaries
  fleet                Inspect and manage Agent Relay fleet nodes
  status               Show workspace, cloud login, and local broker status
  telemetry [action]   Manage anonymous telemetry (enable/disable/status)
  cloud                Cloud account, provider auth, and workflow commands
  workspace            Create and switch between workspaces
  observer [options]   Mint a read-only observer link so a human can follow
                       this workspace
  agent                Manage workspace agents and local delivery controls
  channel              Manage channels (requires agent token)
  message              Post, read, and react to messages (requires agent token)
  integration          Webhooks and event subscriptions
  capabilities         Register and invoke agent capabilities (commands)
  skills               Install Agent Relay skills into your coding harnesses
  file                 relayfile — read and write provider files through a
                       local mount
  flows                relayflows — author, check, run, and deploy agent
                       workflows
  sessions             Relay session history — search, replay, and export past
                       sessions
  mcp [options]        Run the Agent Relay MCP stdio server
  help [command]       display help for command
